WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.000
- Hello, I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.430
- We're the Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.340
- Gav, I was in the Army
for about seven years--

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.310
- Yeah, you were Dan.

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.880
- Which means that I've
got a lot of experience

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.670
in firing different types of guns,

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.720
and just before we did
the "Super-Slow Show",

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.403
we fired possibly the
fattest kind there is.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.320
Big .50 cal rifle.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.200
- We shot the mirror right in the face.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.031
- We did.

00:00:24.031 --> 00:00:24.864
We did.

00:00:24.864 --> 00:00:26.800
- And the rounds were about this big.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.480
- Yeah, I got a headache from firing it

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.890
a few too many times.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.860
- Well, you've clearly read the title.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.610
You know this video is
the complete opposite.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:34.480
- Bit of a giveaway!

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.113
- This is a tiny little pinfire gun,

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:40.800
which technically isn't a firearm,

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.750
because it's not rimfire, it's pinfire.

00:00:44.463 --> 00:00:45.757
It's got a little keyring on it.

00:00:45.757 --> 00:00:47.222
- Oh, you can have it as a key ring!

00:00:47.222 --> 00:00:48.450
- Yeah, you could wear it as a necklace.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:52.770
- Wow, so the 50 cal is 12.7 mil, I think,

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.830
and that's two mil, which
is a hefty difference.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:56.970
- It's wee.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.030
- Look, there's like 20 rounds in here.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:00.570
It's a tiny little bottle.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:01.970
Look at this little bottle!

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:03.530
Most bullets are bigger than this.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.363
- [Gav] You know what,

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:05.760
we're not doing a very
good size comparison.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.780
We don't have a standard
procedure American quarter.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.589
There you go.

00:01:10.589 --> 00:01:11.930
Georgie Wash.
- Oh, nice one!

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:13.140
That's crazy, isn't it?

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.343
I've got sweaty hands, so this
is gonna be so hard to do.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:20.300
- Nice.
- Slipped in there.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.890
- Slips right in.
- No safety,

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:23.890
but I'm not gonna cock it yet,

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.950
I'm just gonna put it there.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.480
That's ready to fire now.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.134
You hit that with anything
else, it'd just blow it away.

00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:31.058
- [Gav] It would absolutely annihilate it.

00:01:31.058 --> 00:01:32.202
- It'd just annihilate it,
you'd never see it again.

00:01:32.202 --> 00:01:33.050
- [Gav] Right, what do you
think you're aiming for?

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.000
I reckon a middle A.
- Middle A?

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.330
- Yeah.
- Okay.

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.610
I'm a bit nervous,
because I've never missed

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.111
from this far before.

00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:41.790
So if I miss --

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:44.350
- But when you think about
it, when you scale it up,

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.390
it's further.
- It's like a 25-meter shot.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.223
- [Gav] Yeah.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:49.947
- Ready?
- Mm-hmm .

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:52.910
- It's a hit!

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:54.610
- You got it?
- I got it!

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:55.700
- Ooh, smells nice.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.796
- Ooh, it makes a dent as well.

00:01:57.796 --> 00:01:59.817
- You didn't get A, you got C.

00:01:59.817 --> 00:02:02.420
- Are you complaining about me missing?

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.640
Look at this, right?

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.130
Look at the sheen on my fingers, yeah?

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.670
I have to pull this back,

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.610
and then I have to like
fire this with my nail,

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:10.940
and my sweaty palms.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.340
It's like slipping all over the place.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.810
It's a wonder I can even
fire the damn thing!

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:17.140
It must mean it's quite
powerful if I hit it

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.410
at such a low center of gravity,

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:20.260
and it still knocked the target over.

00:02:21.478 --> 00:02:25.420
Whoa, wow!

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.246
Gosh!
- It flattened it.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:28.920
- [Dan] That flattened
it, 'cause that's a ball!

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.219
- Okay, so let's go frame by frame,

00:02:30.219 --> 00:02:33.585
and see if we need to go faster.

00:02:33.585 --> 00:02:35.373
Seems like it fires a lot of gumph.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.900
- [Dan] Yeah, in that tiny
little round, it's like--

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:39.763
- [Gav] Oh, there, there it is,

00:02:39.763 --> 00:02:40.990
you can see it streak to the front

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.060
of all those sparks there.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.820
- [Dan] I saw it, it was
in the middle of the smoke

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:45.850
when it came out, and
now it's overtaken it.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:49.328
- Oh, wow, so it's still
a streak at 12,500 FPS!

00:02:49.328 --> 00:02:52.810
- God, that's mental!
- That is really fast!

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.130
I wonder what the, like,
foot-per-second of that thing is.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.950
'Cause that was a, you said it was a blur.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.970
- [Dan] You just have to
crack the barrel like this,

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:03.293
and then in there, in the
end, is our spent round.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.060
So we've got to get our push rod here,

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:11.610
shove it in, and it should
just push out the old round.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.260
There we go, that's the push rod there.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.830
You see, it's got all like
black carbon around it,

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:17.730
'cause it's been fired,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.770
and it doesn't have a bullet on it there,

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:22.260
whereas these ones, let's just
open our little magazine up.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.760
Boop, these ones are clean,

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.410
and they have little
ball bullets on the end.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:28.410
You can see the difference there.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:30.767
I want one now, as like a little
necklace or like a keyring.

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:32.080
That'd be so cool!

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.637
- [Gav] Yeah, someone
walks up to you and goes,

00:03:33.637 --> 00:03:35.561
"Hey, mate, do you carry?"

00:03:35.561 --> 00:03:39.050
- Yeah, I've got an open
carry license actually.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:39.883
There we go!

00:03:39.883 --> 00:03:42.250
We've moved further back,
there's a couple of feet here,

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:46.040
and I'm gonna try and
burst a Strawberry Soda,

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.640
red sort-of fizzy drink can.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.711
- [Gav] I've gone all the way over here,

00:03:49.711 --> 00:03:52.200
because I don't wanna get
sticky on the cameras.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.220
- Bit harder to hit the target
from here actually, as well.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.103
- Is it?
- Yeah.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.003
It's killing me!

00:04:01.303 --> 00:04:02.622
- [Gav] No way!

00:04:02.622 --> 00:04:03.988
- It got me directly in the face!

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.253
- Oh man, if I hadn't had these on,

00:04:07.253 --> 00:04:08.790
it'd have got me in the eye ball!

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.310
- It came out the other side!
- Did it?

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.253
I'm not getting shot by that thing!

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.435
- [Gav] It went all the way through!

00:04:15.435 --> 00:04:16.628
- That's the entrance there.
- Did you go right

00:04:16.628 --> 00:04:18.380
through the hole in the E?

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:19.860
- [Dan] Yeah well that's what
I was aiming for, obviously.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.260
- [Gav] Yeah, I looked
over and it was just,

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.230
it was spewing out of both sides at once.

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.560
- Right, this is what I saw, okay?

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:31.130
I was here, just like, "Fire, come on!"

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:33.540
After aiming, it fired, and I
was surprised that it fired,

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.650
and then, 'cause I had my eyes open,

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.110
all I saw was this, I saw
in slow motion, I swear,

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:42.340
just strawberries coming
straight at my face.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.730
I don't even think it hit the table.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:47.510
It just went, , straight into my eyes,

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:48.670
and on my ears, and everything,

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.090
and I was just like, .

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.590
Absolutely nailed me!

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.423
That's incredible!

00:04:53.423 --> 00:04:55.890
I was never expecting it
to go through both sides,

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.580
I thought it would sort of
struggle to get through one side.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.850
And this is what I mean, right?

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.540
It just went straight to me!
- Just straight in your face!

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.373
- [Dan] It didn't even hit the table!

00:05:02.373 --> 00:05:03.206
It's not even hitting the table,

00:05:03.206 --> 00:05:05.290
it just went straight into my face.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:08.060
- That's so funny!
- That's perfect.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:10.660
- You've drunk half the can.
- Yeah, I really have.

00:05:11.699 --> 00:05:12.949
What a way to open a can!

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:17.490
I think it's the only gun
that's actually comical.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:19.340
It's funny how small it is,

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.830
and it even made a
cheeky little exit there,

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:25.283
just tore through, I've
never seen such a small hole!

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:28.883
God!

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.270
- It knocked it over!
- Jeez!

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.370
So you would assume that
this is the exit wound,

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.410
but, if you push it together,

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.670
you can actually see that
that's where it went in,

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:41.193
and it's come out of here.

00:05:43.596 --> 00:05:45.393
Ooh, just took off, the
entire can took off!

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.100
- [Gav] When the pellet
comes out the other side,

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:56.359
it doesn't split immediately.

00:05:56.359 --> 00:05:59.990
There's actually a few frames
where it's just a hole.

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:01.360
- [Dan] That's because
this is pressurized,

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.420
so as soon as it like gets weakened,

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.150
it just goes, grunts.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:07.100
- [Gav] What are you about to do?

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:10.880
- Shoot a little Lego man
in the face with this.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.760
This to him, is gigantic!

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:14.593
- [Gav] It's like an artillery cannon!

00:06:14.593 --> 00:06:17.013
- Yeah, it's like an
artillery cannon or something.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:21.143
Okay, ready?
- Yep.

00:06:21.143 --> 00:06:23.210
Oh, where'd he go?

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:24.890
- [Gav] He just vanished!

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.130
- Where'd he go?

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.513
Oh here he is, I found him!

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:30.173
Oh his arm went!

00:06:31.251 --> 00:06:32.834
I took his arm off!

00:06:33.849 --> 00:06:35.120
I took his arm off.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.650
- [Gav] At this speed,
when I rock it backwards

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.150
and forwards, you can
actually see the momentum

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:41.370
travel through his body like
he's a full-sized human.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:43.290
- [Dan] Look, you can
see where it's hit there,

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.830
and it's like, knocked his arm off.

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.340
- He's got an arm off.
- I'm sorry pal!

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.960
- [Gav] So this bloke has
survived a Lego plane crash.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.513
- Yeah.

00:06:56.513 --> 00:06:57.640
- And now you blew his arm off?

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:00.450
- I feel sorry for him now,

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:01.700
you've made me feel guilty about it.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:02.950
There's no need for that!

00:07:04.567 --> 00:07:06.543
I think I got him.

00:07:06.543 --> 00:07:08.107
Think I knocked his block off.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:10.674
I shot his hat off!

00:07:10.674 --> 00:07:12.144
- [Gav] You shot the hat off a Lego man?

00:07:12.144 --> 00:07:12.977
- Yeah.

00:07:16.363 --> 00:07:18.060
- [Gav] I think it hit
the front of his hat.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.730
See that dent in his red hat?

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:22.250
- [Dan] Yeah, that's an
absolute headshot there.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:23.490
- [Gav] It protected him!

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:25.430
- [Dan] His earphones
are still on as well.

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:27.607
- His muffs and his hat protected him.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:31.750
It actually saved his head!

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.160
- [Dan] So found his hat.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.500
It's got a huge dent in it

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:36.673
right in the forehead middle part.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.560
To scale that's probably about
a mile that his hat flew.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.023
This is an execution.

00:07:44.095 --> 00:07:47.824
Oh wow.

00:07:47.824 --> 00:07:51.007
- Ah, hit my finger!
- It hit you!

00:07:52.581 --> 00:07:53.610
Because this is so small,

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.600
I wanna get a shot on a macro lens.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:59.030
This is a Canon macro lens,
and this is a PL mount,

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:02.030
so I'm gonna have to do a
little bit of open-heart surgery

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:03.030
on the Phantom here.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.650
First I should take this lens off.

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:10.460
You tilt it down a little bit,
sort of lessens the chance

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.633
that anything will fall onto the sensor.

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:20.783
Canon mount,

00:08:29.508 --> 00:08:31.341
stick a shim in there.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.525
- [Dan] I like how you're
individually tightening the screws

00:08:34.525 --> 00:08:36.540
a little bit, because it's
a circle you can't get away

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:37.760
with just tightening one at a time.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.026
- Yeah, if you put one all the way in,

00:08:39.026 --> 00:08:40.070
then there's no way this one would go in.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:44.523
So now this Phantom fits Canon lenses!

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.643
Get a look at the end of
that, isn't that weird?

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:51.903
- [Dan] Tiny.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.853
Nice job!
- Thank you!

00:08:57.255 --> 00:08:58.580
- We're gonna use the clamp

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.320
just to make sure that
because of the macro

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.940
has such a fine little focus,
and I've got such fat fingers,

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:04.773
anytime I fire it,

00:09:04.773 --> 00:09:08.160
it inevitably moves
millimeters left and right,

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:09.610
but because we're macro that means that

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.750
that's a whole world out of focus.

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.350
So we're gonna have to use
a clamp here to make sure

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:15.993
it just doesn't move, and
I'll just, boop, fire it.

00:09:18.695 --> 00:09:19.528
All right.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.263
Oh my word, it makes it look huge!

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:27.633
Ooh!

00:09:28.584 --> 00:09:30.840
- Look at this, it looks so big and heavy.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:31.940
It's like, .

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.460
- [Dan] It looks like a huge
piece of machinery, doesn't it?

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:37.950
- Yeah, just the fact that
the legs sink into the grass,

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.330
was throwing the whole thing out of focus.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.660
I was having to hold it in 3D space.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:45.600
- I saw you bracing
your thumb against this.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.433
- I was doing this.

00:09:46.433 --> 00:09:48.060
I was like, I was
controlling the whole thing

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.250
by extending my finger
against the table, like that.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:51.890
- Yeah, it's clever!

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:54.923
- [Gav] So this will be a
macro shot right at the barrel.

00:09:56.324 --> 00:09:58.060
- [Dan] Firing.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:01.227
Ooh!

00:10:03.783 --> 00:10:05.870
It's so quick, you don't see anything.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.200
- You don't see anything.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.140
Just for size comparison
in that macro shot,

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:11.510
I wanna see what the coin
looks like next to the barrel.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:12.343
Go for it!

00:10:16.438 --> 00:10:18.152
- That is mental!

00:10:18.152 --> 00:10:19.383
- [Gav] A good visual comparison there.

00:10:19.383 --> 00:10:21.960
- That is really cool, nice idea!

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:24.710
I like how the foresight is out of focus,

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:26.200
but the side of the barrel isn't.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:29.300
That must be like a millimeter?

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:31.530
Yeah, a quarter is
fatter than the distance

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:34.630
between the foresight and
the edge of the barrel,

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:36.880
which is like, about
a millimeter probably.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:40.360
So one mil out, and you've
completely lost focus.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.360
Is it weird that I had as much
fun firing this little thing

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.690
as I did the 50 cal,
just in a different way?

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.126
- I prefer this because
it doesn't rattle my head.

